# SCENARIO: fix_125_first_act_watchall   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: none   BOTCFG: auto
# Fix #125 (part 2) - `wake event=first_act` audit records exist for `watch *` runs, not only for bots
# watched by name. Baseline: runs/bl_b2r 62 ok wakes / 0 first_act, bl_b3 83 / 0, p2_wake_1 21 / 0
# (all `watch *`). The wake hook armed first_act only for named watches (audNamed); it now arms it for
# every audited wake (audFor), and the tick loop checks for it only while a wake is pending.
# PRECONDITION: normal AI, one harness player (p1). Same opening walk as baseline B2.
# Acceptance: >= 1 first_act record whenever >= 1 ok wake happened (expect ~1 per ok wake).
# Offline replay: python tools/bottest/replay.py <this> runs/bl_b2r -> the first_act check FAILS (0).
@srv audit kinds wake,census,cmd
@srv audit watch *
@srv audit on expect="enabled=on"
@srv audit mark "F125 first_act start"
@p1 login
@p1 goto 32369,32232,7 range=2 stuck=15 timeout=120
@p1 goto 32369,32215,7 range=2 stuck=15 timeout=120
@p1 goto 32351,32215,7 range=2 stuck=15 timeout=120
@p1 goto 32347,32218,7 range=2 stuck=15 timeout=120
@p1 hold 30
@p1 goto 32369,32215,7 range=3 stuck=15 timeout=180
@p1 goto 32369,32233,7 range=3 stuck=15 timeout=180
@p1 hold 30
@srv audit mark "F125 first_act end"
@srv expect src=srv:audit k=wake result=ok min=1 within=600
@srv expect src=srv:audit k=wake event=first_act min=1 within=600
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Lua Script Error" within=600
@srv audit watch clear
@srv audit off
@p1 logout
